# sub12 configuration.
#
#   ./scripts/install.sh
#
# writes this file for you with real generated secrets. Copying it by hand is
# fine for local development — but read the next paragraph before you deploy it.
#
# EVERY PLACEHOLDER BELOW IS PUBLIC. sub12's source is open, so `changeme` and
# the JWT secret on this page are known to anyone on the internet. A JWT secret
# that is public is an admin account that is public: it lets a stranger mint a
# token for any user id, with the admin role, without touching the login form.
# The backend therefore refuses to start with ENV=production while any of these
# placeholders survives — that error is the guard working, not a bug to route
# around. Generate real values with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48    # JWT_SECRET
#   openssl rand -base64 32    # DB_PASSWORD

# Database
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=sub12
DB_USER=sub12
DB_PASSWORD=changeme
# libpq TLS mode. `disable` is fine when Postgres is on this host or a private
# network with no published port; it is not fine across a real network, where the
# password and every row travel in the clear. In production, anything short of
# `require` needs DB_ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL_NETWORK=true as a written
# acknowledgement that nothing off-host can reach the database.
# DB_SSLMODE=require
# DB_ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL_NETWORK=false

# Redis
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Auth
JWT_SECRET=changeme-use-a-long-random-string-in-production
JWT_EXPIRY_HOURS=24

# Server
PORT=8080
ENV=development
# Host port the frontend container publishes when running the full Docker stack.
# Point your reverse proxy here. Irrelevant for local development, where Vite
# serves the app on 5173.
# WEB_PORT=3000
# The one origin the browser app is served from. Never `*`: the refresh cookie
# is sent with credentials, and browsers reject a wildcard origin on a
# credentialed request — token refresh would fail for every user with nothing in
# the logs to explain it.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Public URLs (used in outgoing emails). SITE_URL is the canonical host;
# PASSWORD_RESET_URL and EVENT_INVITATION_URL are derived from it in code
# when left unset. Override SITE_URL for local dev so emailed links open
# the local Vite server. In production these MUST not contain localhost
# (the backend refuses to start if they do when ENV=production).
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
# PASSWORD_RESET_URL=http://localhost:5173/reset-password
# EVENT_INVITATION_URL=http://localhost:5173/events/invitations

# Internal URL the backend fetches the SPA index.html from, so it can inject
# per-page Open Graph tags into shared links and the fixed public pages
# (/login, /privacy, …). Defaults to the docker-compose service name. If the
# backend cannot reach it, those pages fall back to a holding page marked
# noindex — nothing errors, the links just stop working. Running the backend
# outside compose? Point this at wherever index.html is actually served.
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://frontend:8080

# Reverse geocoding — turns a picked coordinate into a place name so cards
# read "Otley Sports Ground, Otley" instead of "53.862, -1.958". Any
# Nominatim-compatible endpoint works; set it empty to switch the lookup off
# (the UI then falls back to coordinates). GEOCODE_USER_AGENT identifies us to
# the endpoint as its usage policy requires; derived from SITE_URL when unset.
# GEOCODE_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org
# GEOCODE_USER_AGENT=sub12 (+https://sub12.io)

# Push notifications (Firebase Cloud Messaging, HTTP v1). Paste the full
# service-account JSON to enable push delivery. When unset, device tokens are
# stored but no push is sent (no-op sender).
# FCM_CREDENTIALS_JSON='{"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","client_email":"...","private_key":"..."}'
